<figure class="viz packing-lp-viz" aria-labelledby="packing-lp-title">
  <figcaption id="packing-lp-title">
    <strong>The Cohn–Elkies program is squeezed from both sides</strong>
    <span
      >Sign conditions on an admissible pair, sketched schematically. Any such pair bounds the
      packing density from above; the uncertainty argument bounds every such pair from below.</span
    >
  </figcaption>

  <div class="pair">
    <div class="chart">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 180 122" role="img" aria-labelledby="packing-lp-space">
        <title id="packing-lp-space">Spatial profile f, negative beyond radius one</title>
        <path class="axis" d="M20 14v90h152"></path>
        <path class="zero" d="M20 70h152"></path>
        <path class="marker" d="M84 18v86"></path>
        <path class="curve" d="M24 22C50 26 72 58 84 70C100 86 120 88 158 84"></path>
        <circle cx="24" cy="22" r="2.5"></circle>
        <text x="30" y="20">f(0) &gt; 0</text>
        <text class="tick" x="84" y="116">|x| = 1</text>
        <text class="tick" x="140" y="63">f &le; 0</text>
      </svg>
      <span class="cap">spatial profile</span>
    </div>

    <div class="chart">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 180 122" role="img" aria-labelledby="packing-lp-freq">
        <title id="packing-lp-freq">Fourier transform, nonnegative everywhere</title>
        <path class="axis" d="M20 14v90h152"></path>
        <path class="zero" d="M20 92h152"></path>
        <path class="curve" d="M24 46C42 40 52 34 66 36C88 40 100 84 158 90"></path>
        <circle cx="24" cy="46" r="2.5"></circle>
        <text x="30" y="30">f&#770;(0) &gt; 0</text>
        <text class="tick" x="120" y="70">f&#770; &ge; 0</text>
        <text class="tick" x="96" y="116">frequency radius |&xi;|</text>
      </svg>
      <span class="cap">Fourier profile</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol class="sandwich">
    <li class="primal">
      <span>Primal, construct</span>
      <strong>Every admissible f gives an upper bound</strong>
      <small
        >A Mellin-modified Gaussian yields a Fourier pair whose sign conditions begin at radius
        (1/&pi; + o(1))&radic;d.</small
      >
    </li>
    <li class="value">
      <span>Value</span>
      <strong>LP<sub>d</sub><sup>1/d</sup> &rarr; &radic;(e / 2&pi;)</strong>
      <small>Stirling converts the radius asymptotics into the density exponent.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="dual">
      <span>Dual, obstruct</span>
      <strong>No admissible f can do better</strong>
      <small
        >Rescale f so f(0) = f&#770;(0); then g = f&#770; &minus; f is anti-self-Fourier, vanishes at
        0, and has exponentially little mass inside radius c&radic;d for c &lt; 1/&pi;.</small
      >
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>

